# Bestie brand guide (for AI)

Encode brand decisions as **actionable constraints**. Canonical token values live in `tailwind.config.ts` — do not duplicate hex tables here. Deeper product context: `docs/PRODUCT_V1.md`.

## 1. Identity

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Brand name | **Bestie** |
| Domain | **bestie.mx** (canonical URL: `https://www.bestie.mx`) |
| Support email | **contacto@bestie.mx** |
| Operator | Enrique Batani Oseguera (`src/pages/legal/legalUi.tsx` → `LEGAL_OPERATOR`) |
| Trademark | **Bestie™** while IMPI pending; **Bestie®** after registration |
| Product | Roommate / shared-rent marketplace for **México** |
| Locale | `es-MX` (`index.html` `lang="es-MX"`) |

**Tagline pattern (hero):** “Tu roomie, tu bestie.” — warm, direct; lime accent on “tu bestie” is intentional (`text-secondary` on `bg-primary`).

## 2. Audience → decisions

**Who:** Estudiantes y jóvenes profesionales, typically **~22–35** (listing age filters and seed data center on this band). People searching for roommates in Mexican cities, **mobile-first**.

**Therefore:**

- Layouts must be scannable on phone: large tap targets (`min-h-11` / `min-h-12`), short labels, minimal friction.
- Copy is **trust-forward roommate language**, not luxury real-estate or corporate PropTech.
- Tone is approachable and confident — never infantilizing, never stiff legal Spanish outside `/legal/*`.
- Currency and dates: **MXN**, `es-MX` formatting (`Intl.NumberFormat("es-MX", …)`).
- Launch cities: Guadalajara (active search), Mérida, Puerto Vallarta, Sayulita, Bucerías (product roadmap in `docs/PRODUCT_V1.md`).

## 3. Brand personality → operational rules

| Trait | In UI | In copy | NOT this |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Modern** | Semantic Tailwind tokens; clean cards with `border-border` | Contemporary Mexican Spanish | Generic blue SaaS (`indigo-600`, `blue-500`) |
| **Playful** | Lime `secondary` as **accent** (CTAs on hero, highlights, chips hover) | “Roomie”, “bestie”, friendly **tú** | Emoji spam, cartoon UI, exclamation marks |
| **Professional** | Forest `primary` for structure/trust; restrained motion | Clear, honest, no hype | “Solución integral”, English marketing fluff |

## 4. Voice and copy

### Language

- User-facing strings: **Spanish (México)**. Use **tú**, not usted (except formal legal pages).
- OK loanwords already in product: **roomie**, **bestie**, **loft** (as property type).
- Legal/support identity strings: reuse `LEGAL_OPERATOR` from `legalUi.tsx` when relevant.

### Preferred vs avoid

| Situation | Preferred | Avoid |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Primary CTA | “Buscar”, “Ver anuncio”, “Publicar anuncio” | “Click here”, “Get started!!!” |
| Empty state | “Aún no tienes anuncios guardados.” | “Your inbox is empty!” |
| Error | “No pudimos guardar. Intenta de nuevo.” | “Oops! Something went wrong” |
| Value prop | “Encuentra roomies de forma rápida y segura.” | “Supercharge your housing journey” |
| Listing noun | **anuncio**, **cuarto**, **propiedad**, **recámara** | “listing”, “unit”, “inquilino” (in marketing) |

### Copy rules

- Button labels: **≤ 4 words**, verb-first when possible.
- Headings: `font-bold` / `font-semibold`, `tracking-tight`; sentence case in Spanish, not Title Case English.
- **No exclamation marks** in core UI (hero/marketing may use one sparingly — prefer none).
- **No English** in user-visible UI strings unless it is an established product term (roomie, bestie).
- Meta/OG descriptions: match tone in `index.html` — factual, México, roomies/renta compartida.

